neutron-zzzzzzzzzj-d2d1-mask-rects-256-and-loud-overcap

d2d1: raise the layer-mask rect cap to 256, and report an over-cap UNCONDITIONALLY.

SYMPTOM (user, live, 2026-08-21): "timeline just flickered and buttons disappeared" in Premiere.
Same bug the 24 -> 128 raise addressed on 2026-08-13; 128 was not enough either.

EVIDENCE. The capture running at the time held exactly one over-cap event, 143 s before the log
ended -- i.e. the moment the user reported:

    MASKFALLBACK OVER-CAP n=133 (limit 128) -- bounding box in force

A layer mask of 133 rectangles exceeded mask_rects[128], so install_mask_rects() discarded the
mask and clipped to its BOUNDING BOX, which spans the whole panel. The application's next
background fill inside that layer then wipes every control in it -- the vanish.

The same line also confirms the 11.10-51 raise is genuinely present in the shipped binary
("limit 128", not "limit 24"), closing a verification item open since 2026-08-13.

FIX 1: 128 -> 256. The comment above the array asks for exactly this discipline -- "do not raise
this 'just in case' -- raise it when a MASKFALLBACK log line shows a real mask exceeding it" --
and that line finally arrived. The disjoint check is O(n^2), so 256 costs ~65k float compares on
the rare large mask, which is nothing beside the GPU draws it guards.

FIX 2, and the more important one: the over-cap warning is no longer behind NEUTRON_D2D_OPTRACE.
A silently-widened clip is a VISIBLE, WRONG-OUTPUT defect that needed a diagnostic build to
notice -- which is precisely why it stayed open from July to August and needed a lucky capture to
catch. It is also rare by construction (one occurrence in a 76-minute editing session), so it
cannot spam a log. The other fallback reasons stay gated: "non-rectangle member" fired 5,380 times
in the same session.

⛔ Do NOT raise the cap again without a log line showing a real mask over 256. If one appears, the
right answer is probably no longer a bigger array but a heap-allocated list -- at that point the
fixed cap has been wrong three times.

--- a/dlls/d2d1/d2d1_private.h
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/d2d1_private.h
@@ -677,8 +677,17 @@
      * 128 gives ~1.7x headroom over the worst observed. It is NOT free: the
      * disjoint check is O(n^2) and each rect costs one extra scissored draw, so
      * do not raise this "just in case" -- raise it when a MASKFALLBACK log line
-     * shows a real mask exceeding it. */
-    D2D1_RECT_F mask_rects[128];
+     * shows a real mask exceeding it.
+     *
+     * 2026-08-21: that line arrived. The user reported the flicker-and-vanish live and the
+     * capture held exactly one over-cap event, 143 s before the log ended:
+     *     MASKFALLBACK OVER-CAP n=133 (limit 128) -- bounding box in force
+     * So 128 -> 256, by the rule above and not "just in case". n^2 at 256 is ~65k float
+     * compares on the rare large mask, which is nothing beside the GPU draws it guards.
+     * The over-cap warning is now printed UNCONDITIONALLY (it was behind
+     * NEUTRON_D2D_OPTRACE): it fires about once an hour at worst, and needing a diagnostic
+     * build to discover a silently-wrong clip is how this stayed open from July to August. */
+    D2D1_RECT_F mask_rects[256];
     unsigned mask_rect_count;
     unsigned mask_owner;        /* layer index that installed the list, +1 (0 = none) */
     unsigned last_op;           /* NEUTRON op-trace: most recent primitive id */
--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -437,14 +437,22 @@
          * Note the ordering: this bail runs BEFORE the per-member rectangle check below, so
          * nothing here is known to be a rectangle yet -- which is why the members are dumped
          * rather than assumed. Rate-limited: these fire thousands of times per session. */
+        /* NEUTRON: the over-cap case is reported UNCONDITIONALLY. It means a layer mask was
+         * discarded and the clip widened to the whole bounding box, so the app's next
+         * background fill can wipe live controls -- a visible, silent-by-default defect that
+         * took two months and a lucky diagnostic session to catch. It is also genuinely rare
+         * (one occurrence in a 76-minute editing capture), so it cannot spam a log. Everything
+         * else in this block stays behind NEUTRON_D2D_OPTRACE, because the non-rectangle case
+         * fires thousands of times per session. */
+        if (n > ARRAY_SIZE(srcs))
+            ERR("neutron-dr: MASKFALLBACK OVER-CAP n=%u (limit %u) -- bounding box in force; "
+                "raise mask_rects[] in d2d1_private.h\n", n, (unsigned)ARRAY_SIZE(srcs));
+
         if (neutron_optrace())
         {
             static LONG dumps;
 
-            if (n > ARRAY_SIZE(srcs))
-                ERR("neutron-dr: MASKFALLBACK OVER-CAP n=%u (limit %u) -- bounding box in force\n",
-                        n, (unsigned)ARRAY_SIZE(srcs));
-            else
+            if (n <= ARRAY_SIZE(srcs))
                 ERR("neutron-dr: MASKFALLBACK FILLMODE=ALTERNATE n=%u -- bounding box in force "
                     "(a hole; the bbox over-includes it)\n", n);
 
